# Database conventions

## Migrations
- Append-only. One numbered file per stage: `NNN_description.sql`.
- NEVER edit a migration that has already been applied. Write a new one.
- After any migration, regenerate `lib/supabase/types.ts` and confirm it compiles.

## RLS
- Every new table gets `alter table X enable row level security;` in the same migration.
- Default deny. Write explicit policies per role: admin, office, canvasser.
- A canvasser reads only rows tied to an assignment they belong to.
- Test policies with an actual JWT, not by reading the policy and assuming.

## PostGIS
- `geometry(Point,4326)` and `geometry(Polygon,4326)` only. Never `geography` as a column type.
- Cast `::geography` inline for distance calculations.
- GiST index on every geometry column.
- Spatial work happens in Postgres. Never fetch rows to the client to count or filter them.